# ── banned-claim / phantom-region (base64-encoded image noise) ─────────────
# marketing/app-store/*/03-back-up-memories.svg embeds a raster screenshot as
# an inline `data:image/png;base64,...` payload. The base64 alphabet
# coincidentally contains the substrings "Soc2" (BANNED_CLAIMS "SOC ?2") and
# "+edE+" (PHANTOM_REGIONS "ede") purely by chance inside the encoded image
# bytes — verified by reading the file: every actual `<text>` element (the
# real App Store screenshot captions, e.g. "Back up your memories") is clean
# of both. Same (file, token) pair reproduces identically across all four
# device sizes because they're the same source photo re-exported at each
# canvas size through the same pipeline.
marketing/app-store/ipad-13/03-back-up-memories.svg|Soc2|coincidental match inside base64-encoded PNG image data, not text copy — the file's real <text> captions are clean (verified by reading them)
marketing/app-store/iphone-5.5/03-back-up-memories.svg|Soc2|same — coincidental base64 match, real <text> captions clean
marketing/app-store/iphone-6.7/03-back-up-memories.svg|Soc2|same — coincidental base64 match, real <text> captions clean
marketing/app-store/iphone-6.9/03-back-up-memories.svg|Soc2|same — coincidental base64 match, real <text> captions clean
marketing/app-store/ipad-13/03-back-up-memories.svg|+edE+|coincidental match inside base64-encoded PNG image data, not a region claim — the file's real <text> captions are clean (verified by reading them)
marketing/app-store/iphone-5.5/03-back-up-memories.svg|+edE+|same — coincidental base64 match, real <text> captions clean
